{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Order.Basic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.axkia_pole_T_3_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.axkia_pole_T_3_5","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L129-L134","doc":"**AXKIA sanity check** (axial distance `ρ = 0`, e.g. a balanced\n`T_{(3,5)}` step): non-negative axial distance ⇒ no pole. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.axkia_pole_T_2_9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.axkia_pole_T_2_9","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L122-L127","doc":"**AXKIA sanity check** (axial distance `ρ = -2`, e.g. the\n`T_{(2,9)}` interface): negative axial distance ⇒ pole. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.poleIndicator_plus_one_eq_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.poleIndicator_plus_one_eq_false","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L115-L120","doc":"**Structural lemma.** On a tableau with axial distance `+1` the\noperator is regular (no pole). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.poleIndicator_minus_one_eq_true","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.poleIndicator_minus_one_eq_true","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L108-L113","doc":"**Structural lemma.** On a tableau with axial distance `-1` the\noperator has a pole. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.trivialModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.trivialModel","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L101-L106","doc":"The class axiomatisation is **consistent**: the literal indicator\n`fun rho => decide (rho ≤ -1)` inhabits the class, so no `sorry` is\nintroduced by the §3b-cond axiomatisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.pole_indicator_correct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.pole_indicator_correct","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L94-L94","doc":"**The sub-lemma (operator-valued identity).** The pole order is\nthe indicator `𝟙[ρ ≤ -1]` of the axial distance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.poleIndicator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.poleIndicator","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The pole-order indicator: returns `true` exactly when the\noperator `A^λ_{μν}(σ_i)` has a pole on a tableau with axial\ndistance `ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma.mk","kind":"ctor","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma","kind":"class","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L74-L95","doc":"**Crystal R-matrix Sub-lemma 2.1 (operator-valued, §3b-cond class).**\n\nConditional on the upstream `CrystalGraphRealization R q`: the\n`q → 0` limit of the boundary generator `σ_i` on the seminormal\nbasis is the combinatorial `R`-matrix on `B_μ ⊗ B_ν ⊆ B_λ`, and its\nmatrix-entry pole order on a standard Young tableau is the indicator\nof the axial distance `ρ` being `≤ -1`.\n\nThe conjectural input is the upstream `[CrystalGraphRealization R q]`\ninstance; the field `pole_indicator_correct` is the content of the\nboxed identity `pole = 𝟙[ρ ≤ -1]`, with `ρ` the axial distance\n`ρ_T(i)` (an integer). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma","label":"prop:crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.crystal_realises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.crystal_realises","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The conjecture: every GS normal form's crystal node is annihilated\nby every raising operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.raising","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.raising","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Kashiwara raising operator `ẽ_i` (`none` on a highest-weight node). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.nodeOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.nodeOf","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Crystal node attached to a normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.CrystalNode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.CrystalNode","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Abstract type of crystal nodes of `Cryst(𝔰𝔩_n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.NormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.NormalForm","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Abstract type of Hecke normal forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization","kind":"class","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crystal-r-matrix-sub-lemma.lean#L47-L72","doc":"**Crystal-graph realisation (conjecture, upstream hypothesis).**\n\nClass axiomatisation of `conj:crystal-graph-realization` (the\nBrundan–Kleshchev isomorphism plus the Kashiwara crystal limit at\n`q → 0`). Mirrors the library class\n`QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization`; carried here as the\nupstream conjectural input so the conditional sub-lemma below\nresolves standalone.\n\nThe `crystal_realises` field is the conjecture itself (it plays the\nrole of a `sorry`): every GS normal form's crystal node is a\nhighest-weight vector (annihilated by every Kashiwara raising\noperator). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:crystal-graph-realization","label":"conj:crystal-graph-realization","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/crystal-graph-realization.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}